    {
      "_why_this_component_exists": [
        "ART-226, the AmigaOS 3.2 half. `KEYMAPS:` is assigned to `DEVS:Keymaps` and a",
        "keymap is loaded from there, and a tree ART built has **none** — measured on",
        "its own output: `dist-3.2/Devs/Keymaps` holds 22 entries and every one is a",
        "`.info`. Twenty-two icons pointing at nothing, and the only keymap the system",
        "can use is the one in ROM, `usa`.",
        "",
        "The keymaps themselves are on `Storage3.2`, the shelf, where nothing loads",
        "them — the same shape the 3.9 recipe had. **`tr` is among them**, so AmigaOS",
        "3.2 does ship a Turkish keymap and ART was not installing it.",
        "",
        "**Twenty-two `file` rules and not one `subtree` rule, and the reason is",
        "measured rather than stylistic.** The shelf carries a `.info` beside every",
        "keymap, and `Devs/Keymaps` already has icons — better ones. `Workbench3.2`'s",
        "`d.info` is 1 256 bytes and `Storage3.2`'s is 450; they are different files,",
        "so a subtree rule would take the whole shelf and **replace twenty-two good",
        "icons with shelf ones**. Naming the keymaps alone leaves the drawer as a real",
        "install has it: the system's own icons, with the keymaps they point at",
        "finally beside them.",
        "",
        "That is the opposite decision to the 3.9 recipe's `keymaps`, which takes its",
        "shelf whole — and for the same reason rather than a different one. There",
        "`Devs/Keymaps` arrives empty, so the shelf's icons are the only icons there",
        "are, and `Emergency-Boot` on that CD shows a real system carrying keymap and",
        "icon both. Here they are already present. The rule follows the medium in each",
        "case instead of a house style."
      ],
      "id": "keymaps",
      "label_key": "osinstall.components.name.os32.keymaps",
      "media": "Storage3.2",
      "rules": [
        { "from": "Keymaps/cdn", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/cdn", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/ch1", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/ch1", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/ch2", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/ch2", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/d", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/d", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/dk", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/dk", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/e", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/e", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/f", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/f", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/gb", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/gb", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/greek", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/greek", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/i", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/i", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/la", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/la", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/n", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/n", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/po", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/po", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/polska", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/polska", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/rusd", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/rusd", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/rusgb", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/rusgb", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/rusuae", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/rusuae", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/rusus", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/rusus", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/ruswin", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/ruswin", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/s", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/s", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/tr", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/tr", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "Keymaps/usa2", "to": "Devs/Keymaps/usa2", "kind": "file" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_why_modules_a1200_moved_below_storage": [
        "ART-224, found 2026-08-23 by the guard ART-159's round added",
        "(`every_override_is_declared_after_what_it_overrides`). This component declared",
        "`overrides: [\"storage\"]` and was declared **above** `storage`, and recipe order",
        "is what decides which layer writes last — so `storage`'s copy won and the",
        "declaration did nothing. `detect_collisions` accepts an override whichever way",
        "round the two are declared, so nothing refused and nothing reported it.",
        "",
        "**What that cost here: nothing, measured rather than assumed.** The one",
        "destination they share is `C/LoadModule`, and the two disks carry the *same",
        "file*: `ModulesA1200_3.2:C/LoadModule` and `Storage3.2:C/LoadModule` are both",
        "11 816 bytes and both SHA-256 `35acfea734816965d271352f59c3643963f69c7e4b2469e3",
        "473c5f5a8a60fc14` (read out of the owner's own ADFs with amitools' `xdftool`).",
        "Whichever wrote last, the bytes on the volume were the same. So this move is a",
        "correction to what the recipe *says*, not to what any tree ever contained — and",
        "the one thing it does change is `distribution.json`, which now records the file",
        "as coming from the disk that claims it.",
        "",
        "Its sibling `glowicons` below was the same defect with real consequences."
      ],
      "id": "modules-a1200",
      "media": "ModulesA1200_3.2",
      "condition": { "condition": "rom-older-than", "major": 47 },
      "exclusive_group": "modules",
      "rules": [
        { "from": "C/LoadModule", "to": "C/LoadModule", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "LIBS/Modules", "to": "Libs/Modules", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "DEVS/A1200", "to": "Devs/A1200", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "LIBS/A1200", "to": "Libs/A1200", "kind": "subtree" }
      ],
      "overrides": ["storage"]
    },
    {
      "_why_glowicons_is_last": [
        "ART-224, and this is the half that was really wrong. GlowIcons is an icon",
        "overlay: it declares an override over `workbench-base`, `extras`, `storage` and",
        "`classes` precisely because its whole purpose is to replace their `.info` files",
        "with the colourful ones. It was declared **above** `storage`, so for every icon",
        "the two disks share, the plain one won.",
        "",
        "**Sixteen files, counted off the owner's own ADFs (2026-08-23, amitools",
        "`xdftool`).** `GlowIcons3.2:Storage` and `Storage3.2` meet on 16 `.info` files —",
        "6 in `Storage/DOSDrivers` (AUX, CD0, MACCD0, PC0, PC1, RAD) and 10 in",
        "`Storage/Monitors` (A2024, DblNTSC, DblPAL, Euro36, Euro72, Multiscan, NTSC,",
        "PAL, Super72, VGAOnly). Every pair differs in size the way the two icon styles",
        "do: 1452 bytes against 476 for each monitor icon, 1061/481, 1641/515,",
        "1758/492, 1319/509 for the drivers. So a user who ticked GlowIcons got sixteen",
        "plain icons back and nothing said so.",
        "",
        "Declared last of all, because it is the only component that overlays four",
        "others."
      ],
      "id": "glowicons",
      "media": "GlowIcons3.2",
      "rules": [
        { "from": "Devs", "to": "Devs", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "Prefs", "to": "Prefs", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "Storage", "to": "Storage", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "System", "to": "System", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "Tools", "to": "Tools", "kind": "subtree" }
      ],
      "overrides": ["workbench-base", "extras", "storage", "classes"]
    }
  ]
}
